---
description: Best practices for Next.js v15.5 (React 19.1, TS 5.9) with App Router
globs: **/*.tsx,**/*.ts,**/*.js,**/*.jsx
---

- Use the App Router (`app/`) exclusively; do not mix with `pages/`.
- Default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only when browser APIs/state are required.
- Data fetching on server with `fetch()` and cache/revalidate; avoid client fetches where possible.
- Use Server Actions (`"use server"`) for mutations and form actions; keep logic on the server.
- Define API endpoints via Route Handlers in `app/api/*/route.ts`.
- Use `generateMetadata()` for SEO; `generateStaticParams()` for static paths.
- Code split per route; use dynamic imports for heavy client-only libraries.
- Use `next/image` and `next/font` for optimized assets.
- Prefer `next/link` and `next/navigation` over raw anchors for internal routing.
- Never expose secrets to client; keep server-only envs on server side.

